{"type":"exercise","type_name":"Exercise","number":"","title":"A1","title_html":"A1","html":"<p>In the log–log fit of <span class=\"citation\" data-cites=\"exm-tr-engel-scales\">@exm-tr-engel-scales</span> the slope\nis <span class=\"math inline\"><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\" data-tex=\"0.8559\"><mjx-math class=\" MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c30\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2E\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c38\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c35\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c35\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c39\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0.8559</mn></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></span>. By what factor does the\nmedian food expenditure differ between two households whose incomes\ndiffer by <span class=\"math inline\"><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\" data-tex=\"10\"><mjx-math class=\" MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c31\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c30\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></span> percent? By what\nfactor between households whose incomes differ by a factor of two? Why\nis the answer the same for the median, the geometric mean and, under\n<span class=\"citation\" data-cites=\"eq-tr-multiplicative\">@eq-tr-multiplicative</span>, the\nmean?</p>","file":"ch22-transformations/01-transforming-the-response.html"}